/-!
# The exceptional local corank argument

The residual premise O²(H₁) ≤ K forces L₁ < K and puts the literal R₁
quotient-action kernel in O₂(H₁). The prime-PSL₂ case has trivial R₁ action
and hence elementary corank zero. The preceding radical calculation bounds
the elementary action image in the odd-kernel SL₂ case, and the kernel
containment transfers this to the requested corank bound.

Assembly starts from the full 11.1.2 alternatives and the preceding
11.4.1 triangle exclusion. It retains the local quotient marking and
the two strict-component radical facts as earlier-source premises,
whose discharge belongs to the parent closure assembly. The partial
ClassicalRefinementCase predicate is not used as an exhaustive list.
Source: Aschbacher--Smith, 11.5.6(6), printed pp.780--781.
-/
